# Decompile view: Xbox 360 only

All reading of game code uses the Xbox 360 executable `private/x360/vd/ACV2.pe`
(base 0x82000000, file offset = address - base): constants and call targets are plain addresses.
The PS3 executable is not read, cited or run.

## Fact index first (`tools/acvd-index`, instant lookups)

`private/index` holds CSVs of every function, call, address constant, immediate, field access,
switch table, virtual call and vtable slot (`tools\analyze-x360.ps1` or `acvd-index build`
rebuilds it). Look a fact up there before reading code:

```powershell
$x = "target\release\acvd-index.exe"   # cargo build --release -p acvd-index
& $x q func 0x82821af0                 # bounds; q callers / q callees ADDR
& $x q field 0x284 0x8281f960          # who reads/writes +0x284 (optionally in one function)
& $x q const 0x82004408                # who loads an address, or a string (q const kosi)
& $x q imm 0x38 ; & $x q slot 0x820958d0 0x4c ; & $x q vcall 0xd0 ; & $x q switch 0x8246fc0c
& $x q name EyeDist                    # paramdef / tuning / Lua names for an offset
& $x audit                             # check every sheet citation -> private/index/audit.md
```

## ghidra-cli for reading a function (sub-second, names persist)

`external/ghidra-cli/ghidra.exe` drives a resident Ghidra bridge on the writable project
`private/ghidra360cli` (defaults set in its config: project `ACV2`, program `ACV2.pe`). Every
`.pdata` function exists with exact bounds (`tools/ghidra/X360Pdata.java`), plus leaf call targets.

```powershell
$g = "$PWD\external\ghidra-cli\ghidra.exe"
& $g status                      # if no bridge: start it detached, never inline
Start-Process $g start -WindowStyle Hidden -RedirectStandardOutput private\tmp\bridge.out -RedirectStandardError private\tmp\bridge.err
& $g decompile 0x82bf7878        # or by name: CamFx_sideMoving
& $g x-ref to 0x8285cf68         # calls and data refs (lis/addi pairs included)
& $g rename FUN_82bf7878 CamFx_sideMoving
```

- An inline `& $g start` (or the first command auto-starting it) holds the shell's output pipe
  open and the call never returns; start the bridge as above.
- Rename functions once their role is known (`CamCtrl_*` camera controller, `CamFx_*` camera
  effects, ...), so later decompiles read with names. Output is JSON; `\r\n` in `code` is literal.
- The bridge locks `private/ghidra360cli`: `& $g stop` before any headless run against it.
- Ignore its ".NET managed code" warning (PE heuristic). VMX128 code still decompiles badly
  ("bad instruction data"): use the disassembler for those.

## Raw-image scripts (fallback, `private/tmp/`)

- Function bounds: `py private/tmp/x360func.py ADDR`
- Disassembly: `py private/tmp/x360dis.py LO HI`
- Callers / address refs / virtual calls / field users: `x360calls.py`, `x360refs.py`,
  `x360vcall.py`, `x360fields.py`
- Old one-shot headless decompile on the read-only project `private/ghidra360` (~12 s each,
  output in `private/ghidra360/out/ADDR.c`):

```powershell
& external\ghidra_12.1.4_PUBLIC\support\analyzeHeadless.bat private\ghidra360 ACV2 -process ACV2.pe -noanalysis -readOnly -scriptPath tools\ghidra -postScript DecompileRefs.java "@START-END"
```

## Runtime: Xenia probes on the same addresses

Questions that need the game running (who triggers something, which path fires, a value's unit
or tick rate) go to the project's Xenia build, which runs this same executable, so the addresses
are the Ghidra ones with no translation. List the probes (syntax in
`tools/xenia/probes.example.txt`) and run them:

```powershell
.\tools\xenia\run.ps1 private\xenia\mytask.txt -Seconds 90 # hits -> private\xenia\mytask.jsonl
```

With `-Seconds` the run is scripted end to end. Anything that needs gameplay (a mission, firing,
boosting) needs the user at the controls: hand them the command and read the `.jsonl` after.
`tools\xenia\setup.ps1` rebuilds the emulator if `external/xenia-canary` is missing.

When Xenia cannot reach a state, say so in the sheet row ("Xenia re-check pending") and record
the probe recipe in `docs/status.md`; there is no other emulator fallback.

Sheet evidence cites 360 addresses and probe files only (a probe log line is evidence: cite the
probe file). Preflight rejects PS3 addresses, RPCS3, EBOOT and TOC references in any sheet cell.
